module is_applied_sum.neg_1

// `x is V` on an applied sum novac CANNOT spell -- refused by name and stage,
// not as E_IS_NON_ANY.
//
// The prelude's `Outcome[T]` is a sum, so the old answer ("`is` tests a value of
// type `any` or a sum -- the type of this value is known statically") was false
// about it the same way it was about `Option[int]` before registry 1544. The
// shell spells `Outcome` without a per-instance struct, so the emitter has no
// test to print; the refusal says so, exactly as a `match` on it does
// (applied_sum_arm/neg_1.nv). The pair: pos_1.nv, `is` on Option and Result.

// NOVAC_EXPECT `is` on an applied sum

fn finished(o Outcome[int]) -> bool => o is Finished
